{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Summary\\n- replace the incoming file-transfer offer's single long dialog message with structured scrollable content\\n- show file name, size, destination, and verification copy as distinct fields for small screens and large text\\n- add Android layout instrumentation coverage plus the existing source-boundary contract check\\n\\n## Verification\\n- ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug :app:assembleDebugAndroidTest :app:testDebugUnitTest --no-daemon\\n- ./gradlew :app:connectedDebugAndroidTest -Pandroid.testInstrumentationRunnerArguments.class=dev.telemachus.display.FileTransferOfferDialogLayoutInstrumentedTest --no-daemon on nubia P0110 / pacific / Android 16 / SDK 36\\n- ./gradlew :app:lintDebug --no-daemon\\n- git diff --check\\n\\nThis is Android no-Host UI readiness work. It improves the product offer dialog but does not close the Host-backed file-transfer product E2E gate.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Redesigned incoming file-transfer offers with a structured, scrollable dialog.\n  - Clearly displays the filename, file size, destination, and verification guidance.\n  - Supports long filenames, large text, narrow portrait layouts, and landscape layouts.\n  - Keeps filenames selectable and Receive/Reject actions accessible.\n\n- **Documentation**\n  - Added UI audit evidence and test reports covering the updated dialog.\n  - Documented that validation covered the interface only and did not include a live Host-backed transfer.\n\n- **Tests**\n  - Added automated coverage confirming readable, scrollable offer details across supported configurations.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","closedAt":"2026-09-07T02:40:55Z","files":[{"path":"README.md","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changeType":"MODIFIED"},{"path":"baseline/AndroidClient/app/src/androidTest/java/dev/telemachus/display/FileTransferOfferDialo